{"t": 1793517565.929, "kind": "model_text", "turn": 8, "text": "Lab report:\n\nMeasured:\n- E1 0.39±0.01 m: reliable, no problems. T0 1.24598±0.00051 s, amplitude 11.1 deg, 16.3 cycles. Fit vs zero-crossings 0.48 sigma.\n- E2 0.619±0.003 m: reliable. Warning: 2 outlier frames removed (>5 MAD); agreement 0.23 sigma so harmless. T0 1.58521±0.00075 s, 11.5 deg, 12.3 cycles.\n- E3 0.2887±0.003 m: reliable. T0 1.08676±0.00019 s, 19.1 deg, 31.1 cycles.\n- E4 0.489±0.003 m: reliable. T0 1.39817±0.00026 s, 7.0 deg, 23.2 cycles.\n\nDamping (AIC):\n- E1: viscous best (weight 0.862), coulomb +3.76 -> viscous preferred, not decisive.\n- E2: quadratic best (0.722), viscous +2.1 -> quadratic preferred, not decisive.\n- E3: quadratic best (1.0), viscous +145.46 -> quadratic strongly preferred.\n- E4: viscous best (0.949), coulomb +6.01, quadratic +10.7 -> viscous preferred.\n- Undamped delta 704-2969 in all: essentially no support. No single damped law wins everywhere; period is identical across models to <0.0002 s so T0 is robust.\n\ng: weighted fit T0^2 vs length with offset, using E1,E2,E3,E4: g 9.8213±0.1257 m/s2, offset 0.0026±0.0062 m, chi2 5.53 for 2 dof.\n\nVerification P3 x E4: blind true. Plan 0.5 m, used 0.489 m (2.2% mismatch, valid). Frozen prediction re-evaluated: T0 1.40969±0.00529 s vs measured 1.39817±0.00026 s, -0.8171%, z -2.17405, verdict tension.\n\nPrediction P4 (new, frozen): 0.70 m at 10 deg: T0 1.68059±0.00552 s, period at amplitude 1.68379±0.00553 s. Request sent for ~0.70 m tape-measured golf-ball run, ~10 deg, ~40 s.\n\nNext step: record the 0.70 m experiment to decide if the P3 tension is noise or bias in length scale.\n"}
